sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg micro-ocellus wavelength of Drosophila guttifera at 2.12 µm — MorphoEval overall 80.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Focal linear wavelength is calibrated to 2.12 µm (k_max = 2.88, marginal k_c = 4.96). On a fixed 12-wavelength box the spectral centroid tracks analytical λ across eight inhibitor-diffusivity multipliers with Pearson r = 0.992 and RMSE = 0.208 µm; the centroid sits systematically short of λ(k_max). Equal diffusion (Du = Dv = 0.40) decays (amplitude ratio 0.228, σ_max < 0). Saturated guttifera coherency is 0.010; grimshawi with vein anisotropy 3.15 reaches 0.480; heteroneura at a = 0.24 has linear λ = 2.048 µm. The adult photograph (CC BY-SA 4.0, MA Hanson) segments to 28 dark blobs against the nominal 16 wing spots. Pass 1 uses periodic boundaries only. Overall 80.1/100 (faithfulness 78.0, reproducibility 84.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 78, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_guttifera_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 479439 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 9e62649b8e7299a09073eacf2e1f3badfaaa2a43786da966ef6bdaee8e4c8305 (sha256 9e62649b8e7299a09073eacf2e1f3badfaaa2a43786da966ef6bdaee8e4c8305), spec_fingerprint c4a6d950a832bc4358255a26def4f385a34b6882ca4a5713ae484c2d3f07773c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c4a6d950a832bc4358255a26def4f385a34b6882ca4a5713ae484c2d3f07773c; artifact_sha256: 9e62649b8e7299a09073eacf2e1f3badfaaa2a43786da966ef6bdaee8e4c8305. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Werner et al. 2010: Wingless at vein intersections and campaniform sensilla induces yellow melanin spots on the D. guttifera wing. | Koseki, Tanaka & Koshikawa 2021: wingless is expressed in specific campaniform-sensillum cell types. | Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979: diffusion-driven instability and the two-species reaction used here.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.10, b=0.90, Du=0.016, Dv=1.25, with the spatial unit chosen so λ(k_max)=2.12 µm. | One campaniform Gaussian (a_w=0.12) on the guttifera morphology run. | Grimshawi anisotropy 3.15 and heteroneura basal activator 0.24, as chronospecies contrasts at 0 Ma. | Fixed-band spectral centroid on cycles [0.30, 0.80] and the equal-diffusion ablation.; transfer_boundary: The 2.12 µm figure is the campaign detail tier, not a length reported by Werner et al. 2010. | Sibling slot 3011 is the ~102 µm whole-wing spot scale. This patch is the interior of one spot.; does_not_claim: That Werner 2010 published this PDE. | That anisotropy 3.15 or heteroneura a=0.24 was measured. Spieth 1981 is a head-shape paper. | That the terminal GIF frame is a 2.12 µm micrograph. It is the adult photograph; the generative field is the preceding frames and the comparison figure. | That the global dark-blob count of 28 equals the 16 named wing spots.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Add a zero-flux (Neumann) control and report its wavelength against the periodic run. Pass 1 is periodic only.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Replace the global dark threshold (28 blobs) with a wing-membrane mask that drops the thorax and border-touching bristles, and compare that count to 16 without forcing equality.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Measure saturated inter-peak spacing and its KS/CV against the linear 2.12 µm wavelength. The linear centroid is systematically short (RMSE 0.208 µm); say whether saturation makes that better or worse.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Independent second assessor. This pass is builder-scored only. Left open if no second model is available.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.801"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent; no independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

